<title>ITALY: Cofide buys 600,000 CIR shares.</title>
<headline>Cofide buys 600,000 CIR shares.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Carlo De Benedetti's family holding group Cofide has bought 600,000 shares in another De Benedetti holding group CIR, to bring the holding of De Benedetti companies in CIR to 50.06 percent.  </p>
<p>A CIR statement said that Cofide -- Compagnia Finanziaria De Benedetti SpA -- had acquired on September 19 in the bourse 600,000 ordinary shares in CIR. This purchase raised the holding of De Benedetti companies in CIR above 50 percent.</p>
<p>De Benedetti's CIR is the largest shareholder in information technology group Olivetti with a 14.7 percent stake.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
